        {
          "id": "satoplam-t10-q055",
          "skill": "Underlined Purpose",
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "focus": "Determine the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 10 · Q55",
          "passageTitle": "Underlined Purpose — Q55",
          "passage": "In the early days of television in the 1940s,\nmany people thought that US television\nprograms would rely on the financial support of\nad agencies and commercial sponsors, much like\nradio did. But advertisers hesitated to jump into\na new space,particularly at a time when the\nmanufacturing of new television sets was stalled\ndue to the US'sinvolvement in World WarII.\nBroadcasters, like the National Broadcasting\nCompany (NBC), needed to persuade\nadvertisers to support their programming\ndespite not knowing whether there would be a\nrobust television audience to begin with.",
          "prompt": "Which choice best describes the function of the\nunderlined portion in the text as a whole?",
          "options": [
